   "source": [
    "For your Fake Currency Detection using Deep Learning project, you need to train a deep learning model and save it so you can reuse it later to detect whether a currency image is real or fake without training the model every time.\n",
    "I'll show you the Python code to train and save the model, load the saved model, and use it to predict a new currency image.\n",
    "1. Install the required libraries\n",
    "Run this in Jupyter Notebook or Google Colab.\n",
    "!pip install tensorflow matplotlib numpy\n",
    "\n",
    "2. Train and save the deep learning model\n",
    "This example uses a CNN (Convolutional Neural Network) to classify currency images. It assumes your dataset is organized into folders like this:\n",
    "dataset/\n",
    "├── train/\n",
    "│   ├── fake/\n",
    "│   └── real/\n",
    "└── test/\n",
    "    ├── fake/\n",
    "    └── real/\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Your folders must contain labeled images. The model's performance depends on the quality and authenticity of your dataset.\n",
    "Use the following code after importing your dataset:\n",
    "import tensorflow as tffrom tensorflow.keras import layers, models# Load training imagestrain_ds = tf.keras.utils.image_dataset_from_directory(    \"dataset/train\",    image_size=(128, 128),    batch_size=32,    label_mode=\"binary\")# Load testing imagestest_ds = tf.keras.utils.image_dataset_from_directory(    \"dataset/test\",    image_size=(128, 128),    batch_size=32,    label_mode=\"binary\",    shuffle=False)# Build CNN modelmodel = models.Sequential([    layers.Input(shape=(128, 128, 3)),    layers.Rescaling(1./255),    layers.Conv2D(32, (3, 3), activation=\"relu\"),    layers.MaxPooling2D(2, 2),    layers.Conv2D(64, (3, 3), activation=\"relu\"),    layers.MaxPooling2D(2, 2),    layers.Flatten(),    layers.Dense(128, activation=\"relu\"),    layers.Dropout(0.5),    layers.Dense(1, activation=\"sigmoid\")])# Compile the modelmodel.compile(    optimizer=\"adam\",    loss=\"binary_crossentropy\",    metrics=[\"accuracy\"])# Train the modelhistory = model.fit(    train_ds,    validation_data=test_ds,    epochs=10)# Save the trained modelmodel.save(\"fake_currency_model.keras\")print(\"Trained model saved successfully!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "The model is saved in Keras' .keras format, which stores the architecture, learned weights, and training configuration. \n",
    "\n",
    "Keras\n",
    "+1\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "3. Load the saved model\n",
    "Run this code whenever you want to reuse your trained model.\n",
    "from tensorflow.keras.models import load_modelmodel = load_model(\"fake_currency_model.keras\")print(\"Saved model loaded successfully!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "4. Predict a new currency image\n",
    "import numpy as npfrom tensorflow.keras.utils import load_img, img_to_arrayimage_path = \"new_currency.jpg\"img = load_img(image_path, target_size=(128, 128))img_array = img_to_array(img)img_array = np.expand_dims(img_array, axis=0)prediction = model.predict(img_array)[0][0]# Check the folder class order before interpreting predictionsif train_ds.class_names == [\"fake\", \"real\"]:    if prediction >= 0.5:        print(\"Prediction: REAL currency\")    else:        print(\"Prediction: FAKE currency\")else:    print(\"Check train_ds.class_names to map the prediction correctly.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Important: This example assumes your folder names are fake and real, in that alphabetical order. A model prediction is not proof that a banknote is genuine; real-world detection requires reliable, representative training data and proper testing.\n",
    "5. Where is the saved model?\n",
    "After training, you should see this file in your working directory:\n",
    "fake_currency_model.keras\n",
    "If you are using Google Colab, download it with:\n",
    "from google.colab import filesfiles.download(\"fake_currency_model.keras\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "If you already trained your model, you do not need to train it again. Just run the save command:\n",
    "model.save(\"fake_currency_model.keras\")"
   ]
  }
